link_hdmi_frl.c, above `static int frl_ltsp_mode;`:
Test knob (cinemaONE, 2026-09-26): LTS:P as the data says it should be.
The JVC NZ9 sets FRL_Start after 60-120 ms or 400-530 ms (slow when the
training follows a recent mode change), and sometimes sets FLT_Update in
LTS:P instead. Upstream enables video after ~200 ms either way, and the
screen stays dark.
  0  upstream (dc_hpo_frl_start_polls, busy-waiting)
  1  poll FRL_Start every 2 ms, sleeping, for up to dc_hpo_frl_ltsp_wait_ms;
     on a timeout or FLT_Update go back into link training (at most 3
     trainings), and only then enable video anyway
No status poll is involved: live, its retrain turned a late start into a
hard hang on this single-HDMI board.

link_hdmi_frl.c, above `bool hdmi_frl_start_video_with_retrain(struct dc_link *link)`:
cinemaONE test (dc_hpo_frl_ltsp_mode=1): enable the FRL output and wait for
FRL_Start; when it does not come, or the sink asks for training again, go
back into training rather than send video to a sink that is not ready.
Returns whether FRL_Start came; after 3 trainings the caller enables video
anyway, as upstream always does.

